parent_text:
vLLM now supports NVIDIA Vera Rubin. The early results show more than 7.8x the throughput of GB200 on MiniMax M3 on AgentX.

@inferact, @NVIDIAAI, @RedHat_AI, and the vLLM community have been bringing vLLM up on Rubin since it was announced. Here is where things stand.

🧵 1/5 https://t.co/iN239Tytko

Most agents work fine in a demo. Making one hold up for everyone on the planet is a different problem. 

@mattzcarey (@Cloudflare) built the Cloudflare MCP server and maintains the MCP TypeScript SDK. In his talk he walks through building agents that scale.

Link in the comments.

🫧found a neat CSS feature for entry animations:

you can animate an element from 𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚙𝚕𝚊𝚢: 𝚗𝚘𝚗𝚎 without JavaScript.

.𝚍𝚒𝚊𝚕𝚘𝚐 {
  𝚘𝚙𝚊𝚌𝚒𝚝𝚢: 𝟷;
  𝚝𝚛𝚊𝚗𝚜𝚏𝚘𝚛𝚖: 𝚝𝚛𝚊𝚗𝚜𝚕𝚊𝚝𝚎𝚈(𝟶);
  𝚝𝚛𝚊𝚗𝚜𝚒𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗: 𝚘𝚙𝚊𝚌𝚒𝚝𝚢 .𝟸𝚜, 𝚝𝚛𝚊𝚗𝚜𝚏𝚘𝚛𝚖 .𝟸𝚜,
              𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚙𝚕𝚊𝚢 .𝟸𝚜 𝚊𝚕𝚕𝚘𝚠-𝚍𝚒𝚜𝚌𝚛𝚎𝚝𝚎;
}

@𝚜𝚝𝚊𝚛𝚝𝚒𝚗𝚐-𝚜𝚝𝚢𝚕𝚎 {
  .𝚍𝚒𝚊𝚕𝚘𝚐 {
    𝚘𝚙𝚊𝚌𝚒𝚝𝚢: 𝟶;
    𝚝𝚛𝚊𝚗𝚜𝚏𝚘𝚛𝚖: 𝚝𝚛𝚊𝚗𝚜𝚕𝚊𝚝𝚎𝚈(𝟷𝟶𝚙𝚡);
  }
}

@𝚜𝚝𝚊𝚛𝚝𝚒𝚗𝚐-𝚜𝚝𝚢𝚕𝚎 tells the browser what the element should look like at the start of its entrance animation.

super useful for dialogs, popovers, and menus.

reply_text:
@devXritesh The waste is re-reviewing the whole branch on every push. Debounce the trigger, move a `reviewed` tag after each review, and review only:

git diff reviewed..HEAD

Five commits in a minute become one review, and the bill tracks the change, not the history.
